// Ch12 side errand (optional; requires ch12_ram_felled). The Ram was Dorro's (ch12_bark_herder); his daughter asks
// after it. Pell already tied its red herd-cord on a pass-cord in B07 (ch12_herd_cord), so the party only tells her
// where it is. She is glad: on the road with him is where it belongs. The Ullari way, stated without comment. Sets
// ch12_returned_herd_cord.
title: ch12_side_dorros_cord
location: ch12/quellan
---
Ullari_woman as "Dorro's daughter" [neutral]: You came down the terrace road. Did you see her? The big one. Red cord, double knot. My father tied it on her the spring she was born. #line:ch12_dcord_001 #long
Asha [sad]: We saw her. I'm sorry. Pell tied her cord on the pass. #line:ch12_dcord_002
Ullari_woman as "Dorro's daughter" [neutral]: She went wild after he died. Nobody walked her home. #line:ch12_dcord_003
Ullari_woman as "Dorro's daughter" [neutral]: Then she's on the road with him. Good. That's where she belongs. #line:ch12_dcord_004
<<set $ch12_returned_herd_cord = true>>
===
